    overview: "Contentiousness differs from disputation because a concrete right, property, or claim is involved. Ghazali does not forbid the wronged person from presenting a case. He criticizes false claims, speech without knowledge, needless persistence, injury, domination, and hostility beyond what recovering the right requires.",
