    overview: "Ghazali criticizes forced rhyme, theatrical self-display, and ornate speech that exceeds ordinary purpose. The purpose of ordinary conversation is understanding. Yet he explicitly exempts fitting beauty in sermons and exhortation when it moves hearts and serves the task.",
